    "methods_description": "Participants viewed images for 100 ms followed by 100 ms of blank screen in an RSVP paradigm, with an orthogonal oddball detection task (button press on Woody character catch trials). EEG was recorded at 256 Hz with 32 Ag/AgCl gel electrodes in an extended 10-20 montage centered on occipital and visual regions. Each session had 19 blocks of about 5 minutes. Data were exported as EDF and converted to BIDS with MNE-BIDS.",
